# Deny by default, then allow only what is published.
#
# Deliberately inverted. This repository is built from a working directory
# holding several terabytes of DEMs, checkpoints and run outputs, and a
# blacklist that forgets one pattern publishes gigabytes by accident. With
# an allow-list a mistake omits a file instead, which is noticed and fixed
# rather than pushed and permanent.

/*
!/.gitattributes
!/.gitignore
!/.github/
!/.zenodo.json
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/CITATION.cff
!/LICENSE
!/MANIFEST.in
!/README.md
!/THIRD_PARTY.md
!/pyproject.toml
!/docs/
!/examples/
!/matlab_scripts/
!/pydivide/
!/scripts/
!/tests/

# Never, anywhere.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.env

# Data and outputs, restated explicitly. Redundant against the allow-list
# above, and kept for exactly that reason: if the allow-list is ever
# relaxed, these still hold.
*.tif
*.tiff
*.vrt
*.ovr
*.asc
*.gpkg
*.gdb/
*.shp
*.shx
*.dbf
*.prj
*.cpg
*.npy
*.npz
*.zarr/
*.parquet
*.bin
*.pt
*.log
*.mat
